# The Required rule of the same name holds every other announcement.
# `note that` sits here, because a commit subject uses `note` as a verb
# (`docs: note that the flag is sticky`), and no pattern tells that
# verb from the filler that opens `Note that the cache is cold`.
# `notice that` and `remember that` sit here too, because a sentence
# can describe a reader or a program doing either (`you might notice
# that the pods restart`, `the cache must remember that the key
# expired`).
#
# After a determiner (a word that introduces a noun, such as `the`,
# `a`, or `this`), an adjective, or a noun, `note` and `notice` are
# nouns. The `that` after them opens a description (`add a note that
# explains the flag`, `a copyright notice that is included`). The list
# names the determiners instead of the `DET` tag, because Harper tags
# `all` in `First of all note that` as one. Weir has no lookbehind. A
# guard that reads the word before `note` fails when no word comes
# before it, so it misses `Note that` at the start of a sentence. The
# first branch therefore matches the whole noun phrase, a noun and the
# words attached to it. It then narrows the match to the empty point
# before `that`. Harper reports nothing for an empty match, but it skips
# every later match that starts before that point, so the `note that`
# inside the noun phrase passes.
#
# It hit 356 lines in the measure.py corpus, and 20 of 20 sampled hits
# announced a point.
expr before [a, an, the, this, each, every, another, your, our, their, its, ADJ, NOUN]
expr noun [note, notice]
expr main [<(@before @noun that), (that), ()>, (note that), (notice that), (remember that)]
let message "Filler phrase. Delete the phrase and state the point."
let description "Flags `note that`, `notice that`, and `remember that`, which announce a point instead of making it."
let becomes ""
let kind "Style"
allows "The note field holds free text."
allows "Each note has a title and a body."
allows "Add a note that explains the flag."
allows "The note that the reviewer wrote lists every change."
allows "The license requires a copyright notice that names the author."
